! **Two iron atoms with moments 90 degrees apart on a fully relativistic
! ultrasoft dataset**: the textured half of `MAGNETISM-NEXT.md` Q5, whose
! calibration is `fe2-afm-soc.in`.
!
! The cell, the dataset, the cutoffs, the displacement and every convergence
! setting are the antiferromagnet's, and one thing changes, which is `angle2(2)`
! from 180 to 90 degrees. That is what makes the pair a measurement rather than
! two runs: a disagreement with `pw.x` that is the same size in both cells is
! about the augmented spinor machinery generally, and one that appears only here
! is about the terms a texture switches on.
!
! **What those terms are.** With the two moments antiparallel the density is
! still describable by one global spin axis, so `becsum`'s off-diagonal spin
! blocks carry nothing that a sign cannot absorb; at 90 degrees they do.
! `add_becsum_so` recombines the `fcoef` weighted projector pairs into the four
! real components of the augmentation charge, `qq_so` enters the overlap between
! two projectors on atoms whose local frames differ, and PAW's one-centre terms
! would build two different local spin frames in one cell, which is the case
! nothing here has ever been checked on. This cell is ultrasoft rather than PAW,
! so it isolates the first two; the PAW version is the next cell up and is not
! committed yet.
!
! The state is not expected to be the ground state and does not need to be. What
! is compared is that two codes given the same input reach the same total energy,
! the same two site moments and the same forces, and a canted arrangement held by
! nothing but its own stationarity is as good a test of that as a minimum, as
! long as both codes are seeded the same way and both converge. Whether it
! survives at all is itself the measurement: a texture that collapses to the
! collinear state in one code and not in the other is the answer rather than a
! failed run.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    tprnfor = .true.
    verbosity = 'high'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 1, celldm(1) = 5.42, nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 35.0, ecutrho = 280.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'marzari-vanderbilt', degauss = 0.02
    noncolin = .true.
    lspinorb = .true.
    nosym = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.5
    starting_magnetization(2) = 0.5
    angle1(1) = 90.0
    angle2(1) = 0.0
    angle1(2) = 90.0
    angle2(2) = 90.0
    nbnd = 40
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-11
    electron_maxstep = 200
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Fe1 55.845 Fe.rel-pbe-spn-rrkjus_psl.0.2.1.UPF
 Fe2 55.845 Fe.rel-pbe-spn-rrkjus_psl.0.2.1.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Fe1 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Fe2 0.52 0.50 0.50
K_POINTS {automatic}
 4 4 4 0 0 0
